content.p:
The claim for costs of making 4WS suitable for the Happy Chip’s trade had already been reduced to £53,837, but the correct figure was £32,500

 See [127] of the second UTLC Judgment
		  ;

the cost of new equipment had been reduced to £8,295, none of which was found to be properly evidenced

 See [140] of the second UTLC Judgment
		  ;

legal fees of £40,543 had been claimed for planning permission to use 4WS as a hot food takeaway, and legal fees relating to appealing various enforcement notices;  of this £11,535 was found to relate to the CPO

 See [152] – [160] of the second UTLC Judgment
		  ;
